# Customer Sales & Segmentation Analysis

## Project Overview

This project focuses on analysing customer sales data and understanding customer value using Power BI.

The project includes data preparation, KPI analysis, customer segmentation and an interactive dashboard to explore sales performance across different categories, cities and months.

## Objective

The main objective of this project is to identify high-value customers and understand their contribution to overall sales.

The analysis also explores customer behaviour across product categories, cities and monthly sales trends.

## Key KPIs

The dashboard focuses on five core KPIs:

- Total Sales: ₹139.40M
- Total Orders: 992
- Total Customers: 947
- Average Order Value: ₹140.52K
- Average Customer Spend: ₹147.20K

## Deep-Dive Analysis

The selected deep-dive area is Customer Value Segmentation.

Customers were divided into three segments:

- High Value
- Medium Value
- Low Value

The segmentation helps identify customers who contribute strongly to overall sales and allows comparison of their purchasing behaviour.

## Key Findings

- High Value customers represent 24.92% of the total customer base.
- High Value customers contribute approximately 54.5% of total sales.
- Electronics is the strongest category among High Value customers.
- Patna records the highest High Value customer sales among the cities analysed.
- March has the highest monthly sales, while September has the lowest monthly sales.

## Dashboard

The Power BI dashboard provides an interactive view of customer sales and segmentation.

Users can explore the data using filters for:

- Month
- City
- Gender
- Category
- Age Group

The PBIX dashboard file is included in this repository.

## Tools Used

- Microsoft Excel
- Power BI
- DAX

